# Exact regional tour entry

An embedded Atlas fresh document can receive `regionalTour`, `tourRevision` and
`tourSource`. These are bounded public identifiers, not private study identifiers
or playback commands. Duplicate, partial, malformed, unknown, wrong-region and
stale requests select nothing. The source must match the learner's exact build
revision. Catalogue admission, every target and every stop frame are checked
before the first scene mounts. Whole body uses its existing regional tour union.

A valid request opens Guided learning with the exact current tour selected. It
does not start or advance playback. Existing source/model readiness, explicit
Start/Play, smooth camera, speed, pause, reduced-motion, visibility, retry and
exit controls remain authoritative. A study request, active practice or existing
guided activity takes precedence. The intent is consumed once; subsequent prop
changes and catalogue retries do not replace a mounted activity. There is no new
runtime message channel or entitlement. Nested specimen/eye tours and the
separate shoulder reference module are not claimed as regional-tour coverage.

The initial-selection API is source-side infrastructure until the Website
catalogue and route transport are integrated through the normal generated
learner/Review pipeline. Do not manually append a query to an older installed
viewer and assume it has selected the tour. Website integration and browser
acceptance are separate milestones. Draft teaching is not clinical approval;
semantic anatomy comparison is not patient-space registration.

Original MIT application code/text; no new asset, dataset, dependency or fee.
